{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/380745-attempting-to-fix-firearms-by-changing-combat","id":380745,"title":"Attempting to 'fix' firearms by changing combat","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-01-24T22:10:06-08:00","id":380745,"title":"Attempting to 'fix' firearms by changing combat","content":"I think we can all agree that firearms are extremely underpowered in Scion as we move on to Demigod level Stamina. Whether that is a bad thing or not is entirely up to each group for itself, but there have been some cool ideas for fixes, mostly adding either Perception or Dexterity to the damage roll. To me, neither method works really well because on one hand it would make Dexterity a much more valued Attribute in combat and on the other Perception just feels wrong (can't really explain why, but seeing your target better for extra damage is just somehow off).<br /> <br /> In any case, I wanted to throw in my own idea and hopefully get some feedback. Some of you will hate it, some of you might like it, but I want to know what you think and if you spot some possible pitfalls that I have missed. Two brains think better than one. As for balance... well, Scion is not very particularly balanced, now is it?<br /> <br /> My idea is to ditch the &quot;Dexterity for attacking&quot; mechanic and replace it with a new value, which I am currently calling &quot;Attack&quot;. Attack is the average value of Strength and Dexterity ((STR+DEX)/2) and is only used in place of Dexterity in making attacks. Attack does not have its own Epic Attack, but rather uses the average bonus successes of the two Attributes mentioned (not the average Epic Attribute rating). In all other respect, Attack works as if it were an Attribute. An attack is made using Attack+Ability+Accuracy. Grappling no longer allows you to either use DEX or STR to make the attack roll.<br /> <br /> Damage is made using the appropriate Attribute: Strength for Brawl, Melee and Thrown attacks, and Dexterity for Marksmanship attacks. Appropriate Epic Attribute adds bonuses as normal. This allows Dexterity to be used for damage rolls with firearms without making it super valuable.<br /> <br /> Creating a new derived value is possible because it is already done with Defense Values. I've thought about adding Legend into the calculation, but since it is Attribute+Attribute and not Attribute+Ability (like the DVs), I decided against it. It also allows strong characters to be great warriors without the specific need to increase DEX (although increasing both STR and DEX can make you a much greater warrior). A character who focuses on STR could be as good at fighting as one who focuses on DEX (although the latter would still hold superiority when it comes to avoiding an attack). Finally, as far as I can remember, there is no Knack that affects attacks directly by influencing either STR or DEX, so there is little or no need to alter them to incorporate this mechanic.<br /> <br /> So what do you think? I'm thinking about using this the next time I run Scion, but I wanted a second brain to pick at it in case there is a flaw that needs serious fixin' first.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://emeraldsamurai.com\" target=\"_blank\">Emerald Samurai</a> for my alternative character-sheets for WoD, Scion, Exalted and more.<br /> Like my <a href=\"http://www.facebook.com/EmeraldSamurai\" target=\"_blank\">Facebook page</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/308-skari-dono","name":"Skari-dono","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"104"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-24T22:32:07-08:00","id":380757,"title":"","content":"Seems very complicated, especially when you add in effects that modify either Strength, Dexterity or Accuracy. <br /> <br /> What I suggest doing, not just for this but for <i>all</i> WW games, is taking a page from D&amp;D or many other systems: one stat per function. Dexterity is now your Accuracy Attribute. Strength is now your Damage Attribute and Stamina is your Defense Attribute. No attack will <i>ever</i> be made using Strength. Not even Clinch.<br /> <br /> Remove entirely the concept of DV. The only way to reduce an attack's effectiveness is Soak. The whole idea of a two-layered defense only even kinda worked back in Old World of Darkness, when defending required an action, and action economy was hard to manage. Then, it meant that <i>if</i> you dodged or parried, you were going fully defensive to survive a big attack, and it had a significant cost. Moving to DV just adds gives a second passive layer of defense at no cost, which is entirely unnecessary in a cinematic combat system. It also artificially inflates the (already high) value of Dexterity. So, drop DV. One line of defense. This negates <i>a third</i> the power of Dexterity. It now does only <i>two</i> things, instead of <i>three</i>.<br /> <br /> Remove the concept of &quot;spill-over&quot; damage. Extra accuracy has no benefit. If you hit, you hit. You can't hit <i>extra</i> well and get bonus damage. You just hit. That's it. This negates the second third of Dexterity's power. It now does <i>one</i> thing, just like Strength and Stamina. The three Physical Attributes are now even.<br /> <br /> At this point, Firearms can be fixed just by saying that they add Strength to their damage, like <i>all</i> attacks do. Why? Magic. You're a magical demigod. If it makes more semantic sense, you can rename Strength to &quot;Power&quot; or &quot;Ferocity&quot; and say you're shooting them REALLY hard. You know, like Rambo does.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-25T04:20:02-08:00","id":380897,"title":"","content":"Well, you had me up to the point where Firearms uses STR for damage. Although, yeah, this is cinematic mythology and there is no reason why it shouldn't work. I do have two questions about this method though:<br /> <br /> What do you need in order to hit your target? Is a single success enough? Do you need to beat a universal difficulty in order to hit? If a single success is enough, wouldn't everyone with Epic Dexterity automatically hit every time? That would cut down the necessity of rolling for attacks and we could cut directly to the damage roll. On the other hand, that also means that you really don't need Dexterity at a higher rating than 1 if you also have Epic Dexterity 1, unless of course you want to use your action to defend yourself (but then you could just up your Stamina and Epic Stamina to become practically invulnerable).<br /> <br /> Which brings me to the question of Soaking. If the successes from the attack do not translate into extra damage, you would be faced with a problem of one dealing little or no damage to the other, even if he hits every single time (high DEX, low STR). If your STR is not at least as good as the target's soak, you're chances of dealing any sort of damage are increasingly slim. And I include Epic Strength bonus here. It is a similar problem with the current Accuracy vs. Defense in Scion. You would add damage bonus from the weapon but it is likely that the opponent has armor of some sort. This would likely drive many players to deal aggravated damage by any means possible since that is the only thing that can beat the Soak of that tough guy thrown into the fight, and doing that costs resources.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for my idea being complicated, I suppose that is correct. On the other hand, I don't remember many effects that do modify Strength or Dexterity (modifying Accuracy does not change, since the Attack value only replaces STR and DEX for rolling attacks). Those that do can be handled in the same way as effects that affect Dexterity for Defense Values. If there is a specific effect that you had in mind, I'm not sure I know which one it is but I'd be happy to address it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://emeraldsamurai.com\" target=\"_blank\">Emerald Samurai</a> for my alternative character-sheets for WoD, Scion, Exalted and more.<br /> Like my <a href=\"http://www.facebook.com/EmeraldSamurai\" target=\"_blank\">Facebook page</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/308-skari-dono","name":"Skari-dono","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"104"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-25T12:59:15-08:00","id":381295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Skari-dono</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/380745-attempting-to-fix-firearms-by-changing-combat?p=380897#post380897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do you need in order to hit your target? Is a single success enough? Do you need to beat a universal difficulty in order to hit? If a single success is enough, wouldn't everyone with Epic Dexterity automatically hit every time? That would cut down the necessity of rolling for attacks and we could cut directly to the damage roll. On the other hand, that also means that you really don't need Dexterity at a higher rating than 1 if you also have Epic Dexterity 1, unless of course you want to use your action to defend yourself (but then you could just up your Stamina and Epic Stamina to become practically invulnerable).</div> </div> </div> </div>I was about to say that the difficulty of the attack roll would provide defenses, but that doesn't work with Epic Attributes. It works in WoD, but not Scion. Epics screw up everything.<br /> <br /> So there is a fundamental issue still remaining: combat is a four-step process, or rather two oppositions. Accuracy vs Avoidance and Damage vs Resilience. Other systems model this by having Resilience represented by Hit Points. Scion does not do this very well, since health levels do not scale up very quickly at all, and are not designed to counter increasing (Epic) levels of damage. They could, theoretically, be adjusted to do so. Then you could apply a Stamina-based DV against Accuracy, and get rid of Soak. That, however, makes Stamina the best Attribute, since it does two things.<br /> <br /> WW only has three combat-related Attributes, but the combat system requires four steps. No matter what you do, unless you add a fourth stat, <i>one</i> Attribute gets to do double-duty, making it worth twice as much as the other two. That's poor game design, and I hate it. <br /> <br /> It would be possible to press Legend into service. In-game, it just becomes harder to hit more Legendary creatures because they're able to do amazing things more easily, like avoid your attacks. Apply their Legend, as if it was an Epic value, as a difficulty to all incoming attacks. EX: It takes 11 successes to hit a Legend 5 being. Possibility, but not very elegant, and it just further contributes to the on-going Scion problem of &quot;you can't realistically win against someone higher Legend than you, ever.&quot;<br /> <br /> I guess I don't have a solution, other than including a 4th Attribute as part of combat. Wits? Wits never has done much, systematically. It provides your Join Battle rating. Maybe you can use Wits to avoid incoming attacks by reacting quickly and correctly. Wits then opposes Dexterity the same way Stamina opposes Strength. Make both defenses passive (DV and Soak), combat gets pretty fast. It still <i>heavily</i> favors the attacker, but most systems do.<br /> \u200b<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Skari-dono</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/380745-attempting-to-fix-firearms-by-changing-combat?p=380897#post380897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which brings me to the question of Soaking. If the successes from the attack do not translate into extra damage, you would be faced with a problem of one dealing little or no damage to the other, even if he hits every single time (high DEX, low STR). If your STR is not at least as good as the target's soak, you're chances of dealing any sort of damage are increasingly slim. And I include Epic Strength bonus here. It is a similar problem with the current Accuracy vs. Defense in Scion. You would add damage bonus from the weapon but it is likely that the opponent has armor of some sort. This would likely drive many players to deal aggravated damage by any means possible since that is the only thing that can beat the Soak of that tough guy thrown into the fight, and doing that costs resources.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually don't have a problem with this. In fact, it's the goal. You have to defeat their Epic Stamina with your Epic Strength. What tips the balance (aside from those stats) are Abilities, powers, items, stunts, Deeds, Virtues, etc. Those really are the things that <i>should</i> be tipping the balance. If you want to beat Mr. Tank, you should need to pull out the big guns. Especially because the Scion writers focused heavily (as many writers do) on providing tools to be awesome at <i>destruction</i>, not resisting destruction. It's an aesthetics thing. Most players are more interested in what actions they can <i>take</i> and what they can <i>do</i> rather than passive effects like DV, soak and armor. That's why exotic weapons are super common, and exotic armor rather rare. Attacking is just more <i>fun</i> than simply absorbing the damage. So there's tons of attack powers, and boosts to offense, but relatively few boosts to defense. That means despite the philosophy of settling ties and rounding in the defender's favor, Scion <i>heavily</i> favors the attack and generally the correct tactic is <i>always</i> overwhelming offense. A slight mechanical bias in favor of defense isn't going to result in unwinnable fights. It'll just result in more powers getting used to overcome the defense.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Skari-dono</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/380745-attempting-to-fix-firearms-by-changing-combat?p=380897#post380897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for my idea being complicated, I suppose that is correct. On the other hand, I don't remember many effects that do modify Strength or Dexterity (modifying Accuracy does not change, since the Attack value only replaces STR and DEX for rolling attacks). Those that do can be handled in the same way as effects that affect Dexterity for Defense Values. If there is a specific effect that you had in mind, I'm not sure I know which one it is but I'd be happy to address it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Animal Aspect, Faunaphagia and Animal Feature are the big offenders of adding to specific dice pools, btw. Animal is the &quot;get more dice&quot; Purview.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-25T18:50:45-08:00","id":381495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/380745-attempting-to-fix-firearms-by-changing-combat?p=381295#post381295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So there is a fundamental issue still remaining: combat is a four-step process, or rather two oppositions. Accuracy vs Avoidance and Damage vs Resilience. Other systems model this by having Resilience represented by Hit Points. Scion does not do this very well, since health levels do not scale up very quickly at all, and are not designed to counter increasing (Epic) levels of damage. They could, theoretically, be adjusted to do so. Then you could apply a Stamina-based DV against Accuracy, and get rid of Soak. That, however, makes Stamina the best Attribute, since it does two things.</div> </div> </div> </div>You just described the way stamina works now. Sure, it does not kick in until epic stamina 4. But after that, stamina absolutely does scale soak and health levels.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2447-twitchtherat","name":"TwitchTheRat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2447_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-25T21:51:14-08:00","id":381608,"title":"","content":"In that specific quote I acknowledge that it does work that way, then explain why it doesn't work <i>well</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-25T23:41:29-08:00","id":381634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/380745-attempting-to-fix-firearms-by-changing-combat?p=381295#post381295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">WW only has three combat-related Attributes, but the combat system requires four steps. No matter what you do, unless you add a fourth stat, <i>one</i> Attribute gets to do double-duty, making it worth twice as much as the other two. That's poor game design, and I hate it.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I'm generally with you on your points here... there's a simple way to do this. Each of them does two things:<br /> <br /> Strength does Accuracy and Damage. Dexterity does Accuracy and Avoidance. Stamina does Avoidance and Resilience. The fact that four isn't evenly divisible by three doesn't mean you can't find an even number of things for three Attributes to do in a four-step process. This isn't a perfect fix. It doesn't address the firearms issue. But it at least gets you a more even distribution of &quot;things each does in combat&quot; compared to how Scion 1e works, doesn't require a radical alteration of the rules (removing spill over is the only major thing to do).<br /> <br /> I think making Strength apply to firearms can work if you do it right. I think the key way to address this would be to start by making the default factor in how good your gun is your Strength more than anything else. How good you are at aiming a gun might stick be being based around Dexterity, but the damage you'll do because you're bringing the biggest gun to the party is your Strength. Once that mindset is in, taking it to Epic levels is just further stressing that conceit.<br /> <br /> Take a cue from the Hellsing manga/related media. Alucard doesn't use a magical pistol (though his ammo is special for his targets). He uses pistols that are designed to match his Strength. They fire high caliber and grain rounds with enough kickback that a mere mortal's wrists would shatter trying to use them; if they could even would those monsters well enough to aim them. Seras' first weapon is a 30 mm cannon single shot rifle (a 30 mm cannon is generally a vehicle mounted weapon), and she gets an upgrade to dual wielding twin automatic 30 mm cannons with massive backpacks for her ammo belts.<br /> <br /> Basically, &quot;Strength adds to weapon damage, even firearms, as an abstraction of how powerful of a weapon you can use rather your character mystically forcing ammunition to fire harder.&quot;<br /> <br /> Another way to make this less a strain on disbelief is to dump the weapon list completely and have an extremely simple and abstract set of weapons. Take a cue from the Exalted 3e teasers and have something like 3 basic kinds of weapons (light, medium, heavy) for each type of armed attack (Melee, Marksmanship, Thrown) and have a list of tags positive and negative (pick one of each) to differentiate them a bit stylistically. This puts far more stress on your characters' stats than weapon stats in the first place. If your character sticks to mundane weapons, have them descriptively &quot;upgrade&quot; in line with their capabilities. Your single handed sword user starts with a simple arming sword, eventually starts using a two handed sword one handed, and then starts using a 50 lb slab with sharp edges on a stick. Characters that want to keep to a specific weapon the whole time have a Birthright weapon that grows in power with them and naturally channels their divine might.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I guess I don't have a solution, other than including a 4th Attribute as part of combat. Wits? Wits never has done much, systematically. It provides your Join Battle rating. Maybe you can use Wits to avoid incoming attacks by reacting quickly and correctly. Wits then opposes Dexterity the same way Stamina opposes Strength. Make both defenses passive (DV and Soak), combat gets pretty fast. It still <i>heavily</i> favors the attacker, but most systems do. </div> </div> </div>If you're going this route, Wits makes the most sense. The nWOD added Wits to the Defense calculations for a reason.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T01:08:56-08:00","id":381674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/380745-attempting-to-fix-firearms-by-changing-combat?p=381295#post381295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Animal Aspect, Faunaphagia and Animal Feature are the big offenders of adding to specific dice pools, btw. Animal is the &quot;get more dice&quot; Purview.</div> </div> </div> </div>Faunaphagia adds to Abilities and not Attributes, so that's no issue. Animal Aspect can be handled in the same way as you would handle the bonus to Defense Values (just add in the bonus before dividing by 2). Animal Feature has to be handled case by case I suppose; adding the bonus to your Attributes would make you handle it as Animal Aspect, but that also allows for greater use, while adding it to either Ability or special attack limits the usability so I don't see why adding the bonus directly to attack rolls is an issue.<br /> <br /> I want to say that I don't dislike your idea. Changing combat in a way to make it run faster and more cinematic is something I wouldn't mind for my game. However, I have to express that I feel kinda bad that all my idea got was an &quot;it's complicated, let's think of something else&quot; approach and an immediate switch to an idea that aims to changing combat almost entirely. I am going to sound like a jerk when I say this, but how is that less complicated?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://emeraldsamurai.com\" target=\"_blank\">Emerald Samurai</a> for my alternative character-sheets for WoD, Scion, Exalted and more.<br /> Like my <a href=\"http://www.facebook.com/EmeraldSamurai\" target=\"_blank\">Facebook page</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/308-skari-dono","name":"Skari-dono","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"104"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T02:20:40-08:00","id":381709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/380745-attempting-to-fix-firearms-by-changing-combat?p=381634#post381634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Strength does Accuracy and Damage. Dexterity does Accuracy and Avoidance. Stamina does Avoidance and Resilience. The fact that four isn't evenly divisible by three doesn't mean you can't find an even number of things for three Attributes to do in a four-step process. This isn't a perfect fix. It doesn't address the firearms issue. But it at least gets you a more even distribution of &quot;things each does in combat&quot; compared to how Scion 1e works, doesn't require a radical alteration of the rules (removing spill over is the only major thing to do).</div> </div> </div> </div>But Strength doesn't do Accuracy in a vast majority of cases. Stamina actually double-dips Resilience, since both Soak and Health Levels are a &quot;defense&quot; against Damage, not Accuracy. It doesn't really do Avoidance at all. Dexterity is only opposed by... more Dexterity. You use it to both attack and defend, but Strength is only ever an attack and Stamina is only ever a defense.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Skari-Dono</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> want to say that I don't dislike your idea. Changing combat in a way to make it run faster and more cinematic is something I wouldn't mind for my game. However, I have to express that I feel kinda bad that all my idea got was an &quot;it's complicated, let's think of something else&quot; approach and an immediate switch to an idea that aims to changing combat almost entirely. I am going to sound like a jerk when I say this, but how is that less complicated?</div> </div> </div> </div>It might not be, in the end. I think it's more elegant, since it addresses the underlaying problem a bit more directly. I still instinctively shy away from the idea of solving the problem of Dexterity's value by averaging it with Strength to create a faux-Trait that also scales up its averaged Epic Attribute rating oddly. You'd end up with some potentially strange numbers, existing outside the regular Epic Progression, if your Epic Dex and Epic Strength get out of synch, as they probably will. Averaging Str and Dex together is also going to require a HUGE amount of XP expenditure to keep pace with current progress. I'd have to run the math to double check, but I think you'll end up nerfing offensive combatants compared to the current set up. Using Wits as a 4th combat attribute may do that, too, since now there's a 4th trait to burn XP on, but I think the impact would be smaller.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T03:24:11-08:00","id":381721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/380745-attempting-to-fix-firearms-by-changing-combat?p=381709#post381709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But Strength doesn't do Accuracy in a vast majority of cases. Stamina actually double-dips Resilience, since both Soak and Health Levels are a &quot;defense&quot; against Damage, not Accuracy. It doesn't really do Avoidance at all. Dexterity is only opposed by... more Dexterity. You use it to both attack and defend, but Strength is only ever an attack and Stamina is only ever a defense.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not quite sure from this response if you got the point was to change things. Strength would be changed to a default attack roll for close combat and some ranged weapons (lets say thrown and bows) rather than just for clinches; thus doing Accuracy and Damage. As you yourself pointed out, Stamina's double dipping isn't actually something it does that well. And there would be an added Stamina based DV as you mentioned as a possibility (have dodging be Dex based and blocking/parrying be Stamina based as a basic hypothetical break down).<br /> <br /> The point is that all of them do two things, and one alone can't dominate combat. Going pure Strength leaves you no defenses. Going pure Dexterity gives you no damage. Going pure Stamina gives you no offenses. Ideally you're going to want at least two (probably Strength + one of the others) to make an effective combatant rather than just dumping everything in Dexterity (or whichever one would become more valuable if you changed the rules another way).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T10:38:47-08:00","id":382131,"title":"","content":"So, for a theoretical melee character (very few characters are invested in multiple forms of combat), we break things down this way: Strength provides his Accuracy and Damage. Stamina provides Avoidance and Resilience. He no longer really needs Dexterity at all. For a theoretical ranged character, though, he has no source of Damage <i>except</i> Strength. He is now at a considerable disadvantage. His Dexterity won't boost his damage, neither will his Stamina. <br /> <br /> As long as Resilience is unique to Stamina, everyone needs Stamina. As long as Damage is unique to Strength, everyone needs Strength. Dexterity, which provides Avoidance and Accuracy, can't compete if those get bled over to the other Attributes. It currently provides an <i>alternate</i> source of Damage (via threshold successes), but if that's stripped away and Avoidance given to Stamina while Accuracy is given to Strength, that just leaves Dexterity as the pity-party instead of the uber-king.<br /> <br /> I don't think trying to stick to the traditional 3-for-4 layout is really going to end up a good solution.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T11:52:46-08:00","id":382195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/380745-attempting-to-fix-firearms-by-changing-combat?p=382131#post382131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, for a theoretical melee character (very few characters are invested in multiple forms of combat), we break things down this way: Strength provides his Accuracy and Damage. Stamina provides Avoidance and Resilience. He no longer really needs Dexterity at all. For a theoretical ranged character, though, he has no source of Damage <i>except</i> Strength. He is now at a considerable disadvantage. His Dexterity won't boost his damage, neither will his Stamina.</div> </div> </div> </div>Characters in RPGs rarely invest in multiple forms of combat because most RPGs incentivize specialists in combat over generalists. Characters in the mythologies Scion often do invest in multiple forms of combat. For example Hercules' iconic weapons are a club and a bow.<br /> <br /> Regardless of the numbers of Attributes vs. the numbers of steps, you're going to run into two issues once you make them all &quot;equal:&quot;<br /> <br /> They're either all necessary and combat becomes a giant XP sink, or none of them are strictly necessary and you have to use the interactions with the rest of the system to ensure that all the steps in combat are equally useful.<br /> <br /> For example you avoid Dex becoming a &quot;pity party&quot; involves having interactions such as tactical mobility, or non-damage based attacks be a significant option for characters. By being careful and deliberate in how various options interact with the core &quot;balance&quot; between the extant stats.<br /> <br /> If you go with 4 for 4 option, combat's now an annoying XP sink. You need 4 Attributes to be competitive, where a single Social Attribute can probably deal with an social obstacle. Who's going to want to play in a combat system where it's 2 to 4 times more XP intensive than other ways of solving problems? You're basically saying that being the dude that does awesome feats of martial skill should be less effective than being the awesome trickster than uses awesome feats of cunning.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't think trying to stick to the traditional 3-for-4 layout is really going to end up a good solution. </div> </div> </div>I think you're focusing on the wrong issue. The ratio isn't inherently the source of the problem. It's how everything fits together.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T17:58:54-08:00","id":382540,"title":"","content":"I've been following this and I think good points are being made, and I don't know if I have any kind of integral wisdom to bring insofar as how to fix what we all know is a broken system as regards firearms. Instead I have a kind of question, a related one of course (or I'd start my own thread), and a line of thought of my own.<br /> <br /> Do firearms <i>need</i> to be fixed?<br /> <br /> Firearms are propelled by a chemical reaction and so on and so forth but the simple matter is that that reaction can produce only as much as it can produce. No matter how good a shot you are, no matter how accurate you are or how much you aim beforehand, your 9mm pistol will not shoot through a bank vault door. It can't. It doesn't have the power. And there is no real reason anyone could expect a guy with a 9mm pistol to be able to drop Ares. Even if you gave the handgun to Hermes, it's just not going to be effective. It can only do what it can do. Enchanting it may give it a few extra dice here and there, given special ammo or just a Fate-twisting sense of accuracy and placement, but it's still just a piece of lead coming out at a given velocity to a given range.<br /> <br /> Altogether not a particularly valuable weapon to give your kids. Or, rather, not as a long term weapon. At Hero level (where I imagine most scions get killed) something like a Mossberg would be quite useful in handling the riff raff but the forward thinking parent would probably realise that it won't hold up against the hardier stuff and plan accordingly.<br /> <br /> Think of any military in any monster or mecha anime/manga. They pour on their technological hardware but the bad thing just walks though it unaffected. Only the hero and his/her &lt;insert weapon/power/mecha&gt; can rise up and defeat the bad thing.<br /> <br /> Bows, slings and other bodily propelled weapons would, as usual, default to Strength for damage. Which sucks for the would-be Dex-bunny who would prefer to spend all their points on the likes of Dex and Wits but there are ways to mitigate the need to pile on Strength. Fight With Your Head for one. Mortal Stroke if/when you can get your hands on it. Tactically lowering the bad guy's DV to give you as many bonus left-over dice for damage.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying that the system is perfect, because it isn't. But I wonder if re-writing the whole thing to find a way to add a damage stat to something that really shouldn't have one is all that necessary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2608,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2608-squee","user":"Squee","date":". 01-26-2015, 09:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2608-squee","name":"Squee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2608_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T19:51:24-08:00","id":382628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/380745-attempting-to-fix-firearms-by-changing-combat?p=382195#post382195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you go with 4 for 4 option, combat's now an annoying XP sink. You need 4 Attributes to be competitive, where a single Social Attribute can probably deal with an social obstacle. Who's going to want to play in a combat system where it's 2 to 4 times more XP intensive than other ways of solving problems? You're basically saying that being the dude that does awesome feats of martial skill should be less effective than being the awesome trickster than uses awesome feats of cunning.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, that's already a significant problem. WW never clearly defined a line between what their Social Attributes do. A trickster character pretty much never <i>needs</i> Charisma or Appearance. They can describe whatever they're doing in such a way that they can justify using Manipulation for it. Same deal with Charisma, or Appearance. Why do I need to charm you? I'm so pretty, you <i>want</i> to believe me. Why do I need to lie? I'm so charming, you believe whatever I say. Etc, etc. There's a bit of the same thing with Wits/Intelligence, too. They're fuzzy areas because non-combat rolls tend to rely heavily on narrative, <i>player</i> creativity and <i>player</i> justifications. They're <i>roleplaying problems.</i> Combat, however, is not a roleplaying problem. It's quite literally a <i>roll</i>-playing problem. It has fixed, specific rules. Narrative descriptions matter, in the form of stunts, but mechanics are mechanics. That's why most games have chapters and books dedicated to combat, but virtually nothing on social interaction. You deal with that through, well, social interaction. Or powers. <br /> <br /> So, yeah, being a combat character (that is, a <i>mechanically based character) </i>costs more XP than being a social character. That's a flaw in the system. It's actually hard to see any benefit to your character from having high scores in 2-3 Social or Mental stats. The difference between Charisma 4 and Charisma 5 is hard to define. Conversely, it's super-easy to define, statistically and anecdotally, the difference between Strength 5 and Strength 4. People <i>notice</i> that difference, right away. They roll those dice more often.<br /> <br /> Does that suck? Yeah. But I don't see it getting better any time soon, and I certainly don't see adding Wits to combat as being a significant step towards worsening that issue. Yes, it adds a stat that combat monsters &quot;have&quot; to invest in. Or they can just be alright with only mastering some of the combat system instead of all of it. I'm ok with that. I think it <i>should</i> be hideously expensive to be amazing at every single aspect of combat. <br /> <br /> Unless you either systemized non-combat encounters (which people tend to dislike because it takes the roleplay out of roleplaying, and limits their freedom of action), or move to a far more narrative combat system, I don't see that particular issue getting solved, or even getting much help. No one wants to be told that someone just rolled enough successes to beat their Mental Dodge and now they think their best friend is a traitor. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Squee</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do firearms <i>need</i> to be fixed?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I think so. It's true, there's no logical way for a 9mm bullet to go through a bank vault, or slay a 400 foot tall giant. However, there's no way for those things to be done with a dagger or a slingshot. A dagger would break, or a slingshot bullet would ricochet off, or disintegrate. The wound trauma would be too small to seriously injure a huge being. Still, the fact that Scions are <i>demigods</i> and using <i>Epic</i> Strength makes it happen. Magically. It should be equally viable to use guns. It's an aesthetic choice. The option of being a more modern style of demigod should exist. You should be able to use guns, chainsaws, laser beams, whatever. That's part of your narrative. The system needs to support those options.<br /> <br /> What I'm far more often concerned with is making sure that the magical heroes <i>stay</i> the focus of the game. If you try to bring too much physics into things, you end up with the solution <i>always</i> being to call in the cops, the SWAT team, the army, the air force, etc. Explosives are always better than swords. Sniper rifles are always better than arrows. Missiles are always better than knives. Bombs are the solution to your Leviathan problems. Drop an A-Bomb on Nidhoggr, problem solved. Titan War solved. And that's <i>boring. </i>So physics and reality need to take a back seat to telling a modern epic with gun-slinging amazons fighting right along side the hacker with a katana.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T20:32:21-08:00","id":382661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/380745-attempting-to-fix-firearms-by-changing-combat?p=382628#post382628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, that's already a significant problem. WW never clearly defined a line between what their Social Attributes do. A trickster character pretty much never <i>needs</i> Charisma or Appearance.</div> </div> </div> </div>That doesn't stop it from getting worse by making Combat an even more XP intensive option compared to the others. Putting up bigger walls between the more mechanically defined traits and the less mechanically defined traits harms the game; not helps it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's why most games have chapters and books dedicated to combat, but virtually nothing on social interaction. You deal with that through, well, social interaction. Or powers. </div> </div> </div>Plenty of games spend time on social mechanics as well. Onyx Path ones so far have made sure that such traits do have defined mechanics. It is not something the ST base system is somehow incapable of handling. Ex2 managed a Social Combat system (not a good one) that could be plopped into Scion 1e if you wanted (though there are far better ones worth the time).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But I don't see it getting better any time soon, and I certainly don't see adding Wits to combat as being a significant step towards worsening that issue. Yes, it adds a stat that combat monsters &quot;have&quot; to invest in. Or they can just be alright with only mastering some of the combat system instead of all of it. I'm ok with that. I think it <i>should</i> be hideously expensive to be amazing at every single aspect of combat. </div> </div> </div>The problem with that is that it isn't a matter of &quot;not mastering every form of combat.&quot; It's mastering the basics of combat. If you skip one of the four combat Attributes, you're screwed. Having a 1:1 ratio like you're suggesting simply doesn't allow you to succeed without equal investment. Skip Strength and you can't hurt things even when you do it. Skip Dexterity and you'll never hit. Skip Wits and you'll constantly get hit. Skip Stamina and you'll get squished when you get hit. Skipping any is basically a giant risk that if you end up against the wrong opponent you're screwed no matter how many dots you're packing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Unless you either systemized non-combat encounters (which people tend to dislike because it takes the roleplay out of roleplaying, and limits their freedom of action), or move to a far more narrative combat system, I don't see that particular issue getting solved, or even getting much help. No one wants to be told that someone just rolled enough successes to beat their Mental Dodge and now they think their best friend is a traitor. </div> </div> </div>I think this is overstressed. The nWOD 2e social systems provide a perfectly solid framework for social mechanics that don't let 20 successes on a non-magic roll mind control you into anything, and gives supernatural powers of mind control a place to operate. Ex3 is promising to manage a different approach to accomplishing the same thing.<br /> <br /> The nWOD 2e Doors rules have worked very well for me so far. They're rather easy to port to any other ST base system.<br /> <br /> The silly thing is that nobody complains that Knacks exist that let you mind control people, but they don't want to deal with mundane social influence. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yes, I think so. It's true, there's no logical way for a 9mm bullet to go through a bank vault, or slay a 400 foot tall giant. However, there's no way for those things to be done with a dagger or a slingshot.<br /> ....<br /> So physics and reality need to take a back seat to telling a modern epic with gun-slinging amazons fighting right along side the hacker with a katana. </div> </div> </div>Seconded so damned hard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T09:51:21-08:00","id":383245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/380745-attempting-to-fix-firearms-by-changing-combat?p=382628#post382628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> So physics and reality need to take a back seat to telling a modern epic with gun-slinging amazons fighting right along side the hacker with a katana.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thirded. <br /> <br /> And not in the sense of cutting something into 3 parts. <br /> <br /> Scion is mythic. If you make it about a real world scientific universe, you might have an interesting game, but you will be skewing away from the source material a lot. Perhaps, to the point of invalidating it. If you are doing the calculations to figure out whether your Son of Thor has enough Strength to throw that giant he grabbed all the way to the Sun by seeing how the Throw rules (w/all appropriate Knacks taken into account) relate to the number of feet/yard/miles in 1 AU, you are kinda missing the fact that, if Thor threw something at the Sun, it would hit a guy on a horse and might turn him into wolf-food.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T15:58:07-08:00","id":383724,"title":"","content":"Appreciate the responses guys. I have no <i>issue</i> with firearms. I just can't wrap my head around how you could attach a damaging attribute to something that is really just point and click. Which is, of course, the point of the thread.<br /> <br /> Nice to have my thoughts challenged without flaming, too. You guys are awesome. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2608-squee","name":"Squee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2608_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-29T11:43:25-08:00","id":385349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Squee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/380745-attempting-to-fix-firearms-by-changing-combat?p=383724#post383724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Appreciate the responses guys. I have no <i>issue</i> with firearms. I just can't wrap my head around how you could attach a damaging attribute to something that is really just point and click. Which is, of course, the point of the thread.</div> </div> </div> </div>The whole idea behind Perception for Firearms is that Perception theoretically lets you locate weakness, chinks in armor, squishy spots, and other similar things (Damage). Then your Dexterity does the job of successfully delivering your ammo to the desired location (Hitting).<br /> <br /> But simply letting Strength add to Firearms damage is also a perfectly good solution. It's been kicking around these (and the old) forums for years. Your character is either carrying around a bigger gun, or the gun can supernaturally withstand more powerful ammo that would otherwise shatter the weapon or send you flying back. Depending on how your table feels about it, you may or may not need a knack tax for this solution. =)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-30T09:26:32-08:00","id":386379,"title":"","content":"Suddenly Titanium Tools goes on as many character sheets as Untouchable Opponent...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-01T00:19:01-08:00","id":388094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/380745-attempting-to-fix-firearms-by-changing-combat?p=386379#post386379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Suddenly Titanium Tools goes on as many character sheets as Untouchable Opponent...</div> </div> </div> </div>Titanium Tools is such a fun knack! But I've also seen gaming tables let that kind of thing be handled by Relic guns as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-01T08:48:19-08:00","id":388477,"title":"","content":"Technically, pretty much every high Epic Str character needs to have it or else lose out on a lot of fun scenes. Or it should just be assumed to be in play as a part of Epic Str. Otherwise no one can pound on each other with skyscrapers, aircraft-carriers, house, very large rocks, etc. Or toss them around, use them to impale massive Titanspawn, etc. The no-Titanium-Tools character would just rip out the largest cohesive chunk. And that situation would be the rule rather than the exception. If combat is going to be cinematic, that might not be the best way to handle things to achieve that end. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-10T14:58:52-08:00","id":762624,"title":"","content":"Fairly new to Scion and was reading over this thread and had a fairly simple idea I figured I'd throw out. To me, it makes sense that mundane guns would fall off and be crap once you get to demigod levels but birthright guns that probably shoot energy of sorts or channel your/god's divinity should certainly stay powerful. Two simple suggestions,<br /> <br /> 1. Make each birthright point invested in a gun add twice the damage boost. (Maybe accuracy as well.)<br /> 2. Similar to the above, but scaling with tier. Hero tier they benefit normally from birthright investment, Demigod they benefit double, God they benefit triple. Guns end up being a means of channeling and firing pure energy charged projectiles rather than ranged tickling devices.<br /> <br /> The first would keep them relevant longer, the second would give them an additional 10 damage beyond the core rules if it was a 5 point damage relic. This is in line with what epic strength gives. If this seems like too much power for free you could always put a XP cost, knack requirement, or simply a in game side quest requirement to attune yourself more to the weapon. This would make firearms a easy means of damage (or super accuracy if you allow accuracy to benefit) at the cost of needing to invest more birthright points into the weapon's damage rather than other nifty things.<br /> <br /> Once again, fairly new... just something I randomly thought of.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9236,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","user":"Yig1015w","date":". 11-10-2015, 06:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","name":"Yig1015w","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-11T11:41:51-08:00","id":763288,"title":"","content":"So after getting ahold of the God book i realized how much the above suggestion was pointless. Didn't know epic attributes ended up adding 40+ successes. In that case, I'll agree with the idea to make epic perception effect firearms in general... probably not even requiring a knack. Super amazing sight allowing you to shoot the weak points in the fabric of your target's existence... sure. It's not the weapon that kills things, its the god wielding the weapon. Fantasy gods &gt; Reality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9236,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","user":"Yig1015w","date":". 11-11-2015, 03:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","name":"Yig1015w","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-17T20:08:38-08:00","id":768251,"title":"","content":"In our game we added a Knack to add Epic DEX to firearms damage, as well as one that let you use Epic Wits instead of Epic STR for melee damage. It worked out fine for us.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2123-charlie","name":"Charlie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}